<section class="section section--tide">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2>Interactive platforms</h2>
      <p class="muted">Each platform brings fishers, officials, scientists, industry and civil society together on a single issue.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li>
        <time>8 July 2022</time>
        <h3>Game-changing concept: a hybrid fishing vessel to combat the fuel crisis</h3>
        <p>An online session on hybrid propulsion as a way to keep small boats at sea when fuel is scarce and costly.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time>5 June 2022, platform 5</time>
        <h3>Fishing for food and nutritional security without gas-guzzling</h3>
        <p>The fifth platform brought the Department of Fisheries, boat builders, a solar supplier, the National Science Foundation, the National Fisheries Solidarity movement and fisher leaders together on fuel efficiency: subsidies, solar and sail, slower speeds, craft maintenance and reducing post-harvest losses.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time>Platform 3</time>
        <h3>Post-harvest losses, fish processing and gender</h3>
        <p>How losses after landing fall hardest on women who process and sell fish, and what can be done.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time>14 August 2018</time>
        <h3>Destructive fishing</h3>
        <p>Illegal and destructive gear and methods, followed by a policy brief.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time>2018, platform 1</time>
        <h3>Bottom trawling</h3>
        <p>The first platform, on trawling in Sri Lankan waters, including Indian trawlers in the Palk Strait, followed by a policy brief.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

